The new policy first looks for *immediate* threats – pirates that are already at position 2 and would reach the loss position next turn unless the cannon in that column can kill them this round. It fixes those threats by either moving a stronger cannon into the column (if one exists) or by spawning/merging a new cannon there. If no position‑2 threats exist, it treats position‑1 pirates as the next priority, then fills empty columns that contain pirates, and finally uses any remaining turns to strengthen the weakest cannon. This targeted, look‑ahead ordering removes many unnecessary spawns and ensures damage is focused where a loss is imminent, raising the win rate.

